  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Thinking about getting new tile in your shower? It's a fantastic way to refresh your bathroom, but there's a bit more to it than just sticking tiles on a wall. You're looking at a multi-day process, generally anywhere from several days to a week or more. That's because it's not just about setting the tiles; there's crucial prep work, drying times for thinset, and then grouting and sealing that all need their own time. When you're talking with an installer, definitely ask about the waterproofing system they plan to use and whether they'll flood-test the shower pan or membrane before laying tile. This is super important to prevent hidden water damage down the road. Also, consider the tile sizes for different areas – what works on the walls might not be best for the shower floor, especially when thinking about slope to the drain. A good installer should walk you through all these details, making sure you understand the whole journey from demolition to a beautiful, functional new shower. If you're feeling overwhelmed, don't hesitate to reach out to a professional like HH Remodeling LLC; we can help you through the process."
    }
  ],
